+  2. **Tagged**, when one or more captured tags peel to the revision itself.
+     The label is the project's name followed by that tag's name.
+  3. **Not read**, when the captured ancestry is incomplete. Its statement is
+     "the history needed to judge release tags was not read".
+  4. **Described**, when some captured tag reaches the revision. The label is
+     the project's name, the name of the reaching tag with the least
+     distance, and that distance stated as a count of later commits.
+  5. **Untagged**, otherwise. The label is the project's name and the
+     revision's first twelve hexadecimal digits, beside the statement "no
+     release tag reaches this revision".
